#N canvas 30 30 1340 1060 12;
#X text 20 20 Cut It -- entry point on the Mac. Open THIS \, not main.pd \, when working off-device. The whole instrument is below: u_mother-stub draws the Organelle's front panel and impersonates mother.pd behind it. None of the panel is wired -- graph-on-parent renders iemguis and atom boxes and nothing else \, so every control binds by its send name instead. Open u_mother-stub for the plumbing \, the bench and the screen log., f 94;
#X obj 20 140 u_mother-stub;
#X obj 20 740 u_root 1;
#X text 190 744 the patch itself. Everything above this line is the Mac shim \, and the device never loads any of it. The 1 is the nanoKONTROL's Pd channel -- see below., f 60;
#X text 20 890 THE 1 IS PD'S MIDI INPUT SLOT \, not the device's place in the system MIDI list: slot n carries channels (n-1)*16+1 upward. So it is 1 while the nano is the only input Pd has open \, and 17 on the device where .pdsettings makes it slot 2. If the nano goes silent here \, check Media - MIDI Settings before suspecting m_nano -- and watch for m_nano's own load-time print of the channel it configured., f 94;
#X text 20 810 The Organelle never loads this file -- mother.pd loads main.pd by name. So u_mother-stub is never instantiated on hardware \, where its s~ and catch~ names would collide with mother's own., f 94;
